-7ec6593b0bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{127}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1f43626-2bd8-5da8-b374-7ec6593b0bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=- \\frac{127}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528283} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e0ff4da-3687-5c2f-a149-9fe8a300e152" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528233}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e4ff63f2-f505-569f-8024-44d95016c5b9" :question/problem "Find the equation of the midline for a transformed sine function with a minimum value of $- \\frac{83}{6}$ and a maximum value of $- \\frac{22}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "A sinusoidal graph's midline (or vertical shift) is the horizontal line that divides it vertically in half. \n\nThe equation of the midline is given by\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{\\text{min}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{max}}$ are the minimum and maximum values of the function. The midline equals the average of the maximum and minimum values. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}_{\\text{min}}+{y}_{\\text{max}}}{2} & =\\frac{- \\frac{83}{6}+\\left(- \\frac{22}{3}\\right)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{-83}{6}+\\left(\\frac{-44}{6}\\right)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{- \\frac{127}{6}}{2} \\\\  & =- \\frac{127}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the midline is $y=- \\frac{127}{12}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531860 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1078958a-e250-58d6-97e9-89c10f90c343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531864} {:answer/id #uuid "2375bb02-4f37-5cd8-8f29-71111c06d7f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218