e amplitude of the function $f(x)=-3\\left(\\frac{-2-6\\sin\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)}{3}\\right)-1$?" :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the function to identify the whole coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)&=-3\\left(\\frac{-2-6\\sin\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)}{3}\\right)-1 \\\\ &=\\frac{-3\\cdot(-6)}{3}\\cdot \\sin\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)+\\frac{-3\\cdot(-2)}{3}-1 \\\\ &=6\\sin\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor a function in the form $f(x)=A\\sin(Bx+C)+D$, the amplitude is $|A|$.\n\nHere, $A=6$, so the amplitude is $\\left|6\\right|=6$. Horizontal transformations and additive constants do not change the amplitude."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717564 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cc520cb-20b2-58ad-8f7b-2e8b24fe59cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717566} {:answer/id #uuid "692fe96e-3029-5d73-a538-5002b40da159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717569} {:answer/id #uuid "86183f34-df13-50a8-b02d-29d8ac45dd6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717572} {:answer/id #uuid "8bc1fa7a-7e48-5a5e-83f3-1a8ee29c85bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717573} {:answer/id #uuid "ff5b78b8-28e6-5b4f-88f4-c9f38950d84b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff5b78b8-28e6-5b4f-88f4-c9f38950d84b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717583} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3d07cc3-2445-572e-9083-f156b3e0